{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cfpkz81puhcwahk3X2D4G","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"A scheduled callback gets two arguments. The first is the `payload` you passed to `this.schedule(when, \"methodName\", payload)`. It must be JSON-serializable, and the method receives it already parsed. The second is the `Schedule` object for that task, which includes fields like its `id`, `callback` and timing details.\n\nThe docs examples only use the payload, for example `async sendReminder(payload: { message: string })`. The SDK source calls the method as `.call(this, payload, schedule)`, though, so you can also declare `(payload, schedule)` to get the task's metadata. I confirmed that line in the resolver code but didn't read the alarm code that actually runs the callback.\n\nSources:\n- [Cloudflare Agents – Schedule tasks](https://developers.cloudflare.com/agents/api-reference/schedule-tasks/)\n- [cloudflare/agents source (index.ts)](https://github.com/cloudflare/agents/blob/main/packages/agents/src/index.ts)"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":564,"cache_read_input_tokens":4584,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":564},"output_tokens":328,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"cc21058a-3d76-4fb8-8df2-74d89bc4014b","uuid":"db6cf044-a167-46d1-8da8-e145dac89258","timestamp":"2026-10-08T12:20:13.737Z","request_id":"req_011Cfpkz7kwwSTWL9w8swSJM"}
